<section class="privacy" id="privacy">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">Privacy</span>
      <h2>Your data stays yours. Here's how.</h2>
      <p>Most assistants ship your voice to a data centre and ask you to trust the policy. Ari mostly doesn't need to — and when something does use the internet, it says so.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="tenets">
      <div class="tenet">
        <div class="n">On your device</div>
        <h3>The thinking happens here</h3>
        <p>The listening, the transcribing, and the working-out-what-you-meant all happen on your phone. The internet is optional.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="tenet">
        <div class="n">Opt-in cloud</div>
        <h3>You decide what leaves</h3>
        <p>Want to plug in ChatGPT or Claude? Go for it — but that's your call, and every skill is upfront about when it uses the network.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="tenet">
        <div class="n">Open source</div>
        <h3>Don't just take our word</h3>
        <p>Every line is out in the open. Read the code, check the claims, or fork the lot.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="band-cta"><a href="/privacy">Read the whole privacy story →</a></p>
  </div>
</section>
